@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Convert PDF to Excel Online Free";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Convert PDF to EXCEL online for free. Fast and secure PDF to EXCEL converter.";
}
<head>
  <script async src="https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js?client=ca-pub-8899635585691076"
     crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
</head>
<div class="container py-5 d-flex justify-content-center">
    <div class="card shadow-lg p-5" style="max-width: 500px; width: 100%;">
        <div class="card-body text-center">
            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">Convert PDF to Excel</h2>
            <p class="text-muted mb-4">Upload a PDF and get its text extracted into an Excel file.</p>

            @if (!ViewData.ModelState.IsValid)
            {
                <div class="alert alert-danger text-start">
                    @foreach (var error in ViewData.ModelState.Values.SelectMany(v => v.Errors))
                    {
                        <div>@error.ErrorMessage</div>
                    }
                </div>
            }

            <form asp-action="PdfToExcel" method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data" id="pdfToXlForm">
                <input type="file" name="file" class="form-control mb-3" accept="application/pdf">
                <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary w-100">
                    <i class="bi bi-file-earmark-spreadsheet-fill me-2"></i> Convert to Excel
                </button>
            </form>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<section class="related-tools">
  <h3>Related Tools</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/PDF/ExcelToPdf">Excel to PDF</a></li>
    <li><a href="/PDF/PdfToDoc">PDF to Word</a></li>
    <li><a href="/PDF/Compress">Compress PDF</a></li>
  </ul>
</section>
<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="card shadow-sm p-4" style="border-radius: 12px;">
        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">How to Convert PDF to Excel Online</h2>

           <p>
        Handling data in PDF files can be challenging, especially when you need to analyze or reuse it in Excel. Our <strong>PDF to Excel converter online</strong> allows you to quickly and securely extract tables, text, and structured data from PDF files into editable XLSX or XLS spreadsheets. With accurate conversion and preserved formatting, you can start working with your data immediately, without manually copying or reformatting.
    </p>

    <h2 class="fw-semibold mt-5">Introduction</h2>

    <p>
        PDF files are commonly used for reports, invoices, financial statements, and forms because they maintain consistent formatting across devices. However, extracting tables or structured data from PDFs can be time-consuming and prone to errors if done manually. Converting PDFs into Excel spreadsheets makes it easier to analyze, sort, filter, and manipulate data efficiently.
    </p>

    <p>
        Our online PDF to Excel converter eliminates the need for complex desktop software or technical knowledge. It works directly in your browser on Windows, Mac, Android, or iOS devices. Whether you’re a business professional, accountant, student, or data analyst, this tool simplifies the process of turning PDF data into actionable Excel spreadsheets.
    </p>

    <p>
        The conversion process preserves table structures, text alignment, and numeric data accuracy, ensuring your Excel file is ready to use immediately.
    </p>

    <h2 class="fw-semibold mt-5">Step-by-Step Guide to Convert PDF to Excel</h2>

    <p>
        Converting PDF files to Excel is simple and can be done in just a few clicks. Follow this step-by-step guide:
    </p>

    <ol class="mb-4">
        <li>
            <strong>Upload your PDF file:</strong> Click the upload area or drag and drop your PDF into the designated box. You can select files from your computer, tablet, or smartphone.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Click “Convert to Excel”:</strong> Start the conversion process. Our tool accurately detects tables, rows, and columns, and transfers them into XLSX or XLS format.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Download your Excel file:</strong> Once the conversion is complete, download your spreadsheet instantly. Open it in Microsoft Excel, Google Sheets, or any Excel-compatible application to start analyzing your data.
        </li>
    </ol>

    <p>
        The entire process is fast, browser-based, and requires no registration or software installation.
    </p>

